      <div type="clause" n="37.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 37.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="37.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="70" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he hit butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.18"/> his gewitnesse do<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.14"/>, geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.19"/> se þe hine to men feormie CXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.20"/> scill. to wite: dæle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.21"/> he hwæðre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.22"/> ðæt, healf cyninge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.23"/> in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.24"/> ða scire ðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.25"/> he ǽr folgode, healf in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.24"/> þa ðe he oncymð.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="37.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="70" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he hit buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.1"/> his gewitnesse dó, gesylle se þe hyne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.2"/> to men feormige CXX scll' to wite: dæle he þæt hweðre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.8"/>, healf (þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.9"/>) cyninge on ða scire ðe he ær folgode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.10"/> (⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.9"/>) healf on ða ðe he (þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.9"/>) oncymð.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="37.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="70" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he hit buton his g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>witnysse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.5"/> dó, gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.6"/> [se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.7"/> ðe] hine to men feormie, hundtwelftig scill' to wite: dæle hé hwæðere þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi>, healf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.8-3"/> cyninge in þa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.9-3"/> scire þe he ær folgode, healf in þa þe he [on]cymð.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.10-3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="37.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="71" ed="#liebermann"/>Si preter licentiam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.8-2"/> illius abscedat: qui eum in hominem susceperit, CXX solidos forisfacture reddat. Diuidatur tamen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.9-2"/> hoc, dimidium regi in comitatu quo ante seruiuit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.10-2"/> (incoluit), dimidium (uero<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.11"/>) in eum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.12"/> quo uenerit.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.oe.13"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="80" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif he hit butan his gewitnesse do, geselle se þe hine to men feormie CXX scill. to wite: dæle he hwæðre ðæt, healf cyninge<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Af_37-1.attnote.fn.11"/> in<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Af_37-1.attnote.fn.12"/> ða scire ðe he ǽr folgode, [⁊]<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Af_37-1.attnote.fn.13"/> healf in þa ðe he oncymð<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Af_37-1.attnote.fn.14"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="38.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="336" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif he hit butan his gewitnesse do, geselle se þe hine to men feormie CXX scill to wite: dæle he hwæðre ðæt, healf cyninge in ða scire ðe he ǽr folgode, healf in þa ðe he oncymð.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="71" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn er es ohne dessen Zeugniss thut, so zahle der [Herr], welcher ihn zum Manne aufnimmt, 120 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.de.1"/> zur Strafe: und zwar vertheile er dies dem Könige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.de.2"/> halb<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.de.3"/> in die Grafschaft, welcher jener [Mann] bisher untergeben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.de.4"/> war, und halb in die, in welche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_37-1.lnote.de.5"/> derselbe [jetzt] hinkommt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If he does it without his witness, let the [lord] who takes him on as his man pay 120 shillings as a fine: and indeed let him divide this for the king, half into the shire to which that [man] was hitherto subject, and half into the one into which he [now] comes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="81" ed="#attenborough"/>If he does so without his cognisance, he who takes him into his employment shall pay a fine of 120 shillings; but he shall divide the payment, [paying] half to the king<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_37-1.attnote.n.1"/> in the district where the man has been residing<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_37-1.attnote.n.2"/>, and half in that to which he has come.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="415" ed="#whitelock"/>If he do it without his witness, he who accepts him as his man is to pay 120 shillings compensation; he is, however, to divide it, half to the king in the shire in which the man served previously, half in that into which he has come.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="337" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If he does it without his knowledge, let him who took him on as his man pay 120 shillings as fine: however, he should divide that, half to the [lord] in the shire he belonged to before and half to [the lord] in that [shire] where he has arrived.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="337"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_39">Ine 39</ref> <quote>Ine §40 requires that the man himself, not the lord, pay the fine: 60 shillings to his first lord.</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_37-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton his gewitnysse dó <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton his gewitnysse dó Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_37-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dó <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dó So</seg></note>
